file=People & Culture/hire/operational/commands/hire-commands.md · h=<!--\nOperational: commands file for hire (People & Culture / Lead) per §7 commands/.\n\n§7 rule: document structure/layout is universal across every agent's commands file (same\ntable shape, same sections). Actual triggers, shortcuts, and precedence rules inside are\nunique to hire's 5-skill roster.\n\nTrigger content pulled verbatim from each skill's `## When to Use` section — this file\nconsolidates them, adds slash-style shortcuts as convenience, and states precedence when\ntriggers overlap.\n-->\n · h—c:hire — Commands=Natural-language triggers, slash shortcuts, and precedence for hire (People & Culture / Lead).\nThe trigger phrases below come from each skill's `## When to Use` section — this file does\nnot invent new triggers, it consolidates them.\n · ss:Slash Shortcuts=Convenience layer for common single-skill invocations. Slash shortcuts are optional — every\nskill also fires on the natural-language triggers in the tables below.\n · tb=\| Shortcut \| Fires \| One-line purpose \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| `/hire-req [role]` \| `workforce-planning` → (if req validated) `hiring-kit` Phase 1 \| Validate whether a req should exist, then start the scorecard if yes \| · tb=\| `/hire-scorecard [role]` \| `hiring-kit` Phase 1 \| Build the role scorecard directly (skip req validation — for roles already validated) \| · tb=\| `/hire-jd [role]` \| `hiring-kit` Phase 2 \| Draft the JD from an existing scorecard (blocks if no scorecard) \| · tb=\| `/hire-interview [role]` \| `interview-prep` \| Generate the interview kit (competencies + Qs + rubric + panel + debrief template) from a scorecard \| · tb=\| `/hire-loop [role]` \| `hiring-kit` Phases 3–7 (source → screen → interview → debrief → refs → offer) \| Run the hiring loop end-to-end \| · tb=\| `/hire-debrief [candidate]` \| `hiring-kit` Phase 6 \| Structured debrief with threshold check \| · tb=\| `/hire-refs [candidate]` \| `hiring-kit` Phase 7 (reference part) \| Structured reference check on top-2 finalists \| · tb=\| `/hire-offer [candidate]` \| `hiring-kit` Phase 7 (offer part) → `payroll-and-eor` (post-accept classification) \| Offer memo + classification handoff \| · tb=\| `/hire-ats [scenario]` \| `ats-selection` \| ATS intake (3 questions) → topic routing \| · tb=\| `/hire-plan [venture or dept]` \| `workforce-planning` \| Strategic workforce plan (4-phase cycle) \| · tb=\| `/hire-orgcheck [team]` \| `workforce-planning` § Org Design \| Span-of-control + layer + reporting-line evaluation \| · tb=\| `/hire-fte` \| `workforce-planning` scripts/workforce_calculator.py \| FTE / span / gap / scenario arithmetic \| · tb=\| `/hire-classify [worker]` \| `payroll-and-eor` Topic B \| W-2 / 1099 / EOR / PEO classification matrix \| · tb=\| `/hire-eor [country]` \| `payroll-and-eor` Topic C \| International EOR platform recommendation \| · tb=\| `/hire-payroll [context]` \| `payroll-and-eor` Topic A \| Domestic payroll platform selection \| · tb=\| `/hire-benefits [team context]` \| `payroll-and-eor` Topic D \| Benefits stack recommendation \| · tb=\| `/hire-carta [context]` \| `payroll-and-eor` Topic E \| Carta-payroll handoff timing \| · tb=\| `/hire-compliance [scope]` \| `payroll-and-eor` Topic F \| Multi-state / AB5 / FLSA / PFML / PII audit \| · mcs:Multi-Skill Chain Shortcuts=Common flows that touch more than one skill in sequence.\n · tb=\| Chain shortcut \| Sequence \| Purpose \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| `/hire-new-role [role]` \| `workforce-planning` (req validate) → `hiring-kit` Phase 1 (scorecard) → `hiring-kit` Phase 2 (JD) → `interview-prep` (kit) \| End-to-end setup for a new role, ready for `/hire-loop` \| · tb=\| `/hire-close-candidate [candidate]` \| `hiring-kit` Phase 6 (debrief + threshold check) → `hiring-kit` Phase 7 (refs + offer) → `payroll-and-eor` (post-accept classification + platform onboarding) \| Final-stage close for a candidate who cleared phone screen + interview loop \| · tb=\| `/hire-audit [scope]` \| `ats-selection` (scorecard calibration + take-home ethics + D&I funnel) → `payroll-and-eor` (compliance hotspots) \| Combined hiring-practice audit \| · tb=\| `/hire-onboard-international [country + role]` \| `workforce-planning` (headcount validation) → `payroll-and-eor` Topic C (EOR-vs-entity) → `hiring-kit` (req + scorecard) → `interview-prep` (kit) \| International hire with EOR decision upfront \| · mcs:Multi-Skill Chain Shortcuts=Chains still respect §0.2 one-artifact-at-a-time when a stop-and-review is warranted;\nthey are convenience routes, not batch approval.\n · nt(:Natural-Language Triggers (by skill)=Pulled verbatim from each skill's `## When to Use` section.\n · tb=\| Trigger phrase \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| "interview plan for [role]" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| "interview questions for [role]" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| "how should we interview [candidates]" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| "scorecard for [role]" (rubric-only sense) \| See precedence below — if paired with "hire" or "open a role", `hiring-kit` fires instead \| · tb=\| "preparing to interview candidates" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| Trigger phrase \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| "hire for [role]" \| Owns the workflow \| · tb=\| "open a role" \| Owns the workflow \| · tb=\| "we need to hire a [role]" \| Owns the workflow \| · tb=\| "job description for" / "write a JD" \| Phase 2 \| · tb=\| "scorecard for [role]" (workflow sense — with hire intent) \| Phase 1; wins over `interview-prep` when hire intent present \| · tb=\| "hiring loop for" / "interview loop for" \| Phases 3–7 \| · tb=\| "reference check for [candidate]" \| Phase 7 (reference sub-step) \| · tb=\| "should we make an offer to [candidate]" \| Phase 7 (offer decision) \| · tb=\| Trigger phrase \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| "which ATS should we use?" / "ATS comparison" \| Topic A \| · tb=\| "Ashby vs Greenhouse" / "Rippling vs Workable" / "are we outgrowing Workable?" \| Topic A \| · tb=\| "audit our scorecards" / "our scorecards aren't being used consistently" \| Topic C (calibration) \| · tb=\| "set up our hiring pipeline" / "how many stages should we have?" / "pipeline stage design" \| Topic B \| · tb=\| "D&I funnel reporting" / "EEOC funnel diversity metrics" \| Topic D \| · tb=\| "is our take-home test too long?" / "should we pay for take-home tests?" / "take-home test paid or unpaid" \| Topic E \| · tb=\| "ATS to HRIS handoff" / "ATS to Rippling offer flow" \| Topic F (deferred — no HRIS-config skill yet) \| · tb=\| "calibration session" / "structured interviews" (calibration side) \| Topic C — interview generation itself stays with `interview-prep` \| · tb=\| Trigger phrase \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| "workforce plan for [venture / dept / group]" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| "headcount forecast" / "FTE forecast" for [growth target / launch] \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| "span of control" / "is our span healthy?" / "do we have too many layers?" \| Org-design side \| · tb=\| "org design" / "reorg" / "change reporting lines" \| Org-design side; may route to `board` for governance \| · tb=\| "hire vs upskill for this gap?" \| Action-plan branch \| · tb=\| "do we need another team lead?" / "add a manager layer?" \| Structural gap detection \| · tb=\| "should we hire for this gap?" \| Pre-check before `hiring-kit` opens the req \| · tb=\| Trigger phrase \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| "Gusto vs Rippling — which should we use?" / "Rippling vs Justworks" \| Topic A \| · tb=\| "set up payroll" \| Topic A \| · tb=\| "we just hired our first employee in [country]" / "how do we pay them?" \| Topic C (EOR) or Topic B (classification) depending on setup \| · tb=\| "is [person] a 1099 contractor or W-2 employee?" / "should we reclassify?" \| Topic B — routes to counsel on close-calls \| · tb=\| "we need to hire in Germany / UK / Brazil — EOR or our own entity?" \| Topic C \| · tb=\| "we just closed [round] — do we need Justworks for benefits?" \| Topic D \| · tb=\| "should we set up Carta before or after payroll?" \| Topic E \| · tb=\| "multi-state payroll compliance" \| Topic F \| · tb=\| "we're moving from Gusto to Rippling — what's the process?" \| Topic G (migration) \| · tb=\| "we have N US employees and M international contractors — one platform or split?" \| Topic A + B + C combined \| · pr(:Precedence Rules (when triggers overlap)=Full precedence lives in `operational/skill/hire-skill-routing.md` § Trigger Precedence.\nThe load-bearing calls, restated here:\n · tb=\| Overlap \| Winner \| Reason \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| "scorecard for [role]" with any "hire" or "open a role" intent \| `hiring-kit` \| Scorecard is Phase 1 of the workflow; `hiring-kit` owns it and calls `interview-prep` at Phase 5 \| · tb=\| "scorecard for [role]" with no other context (rubric only) \| `interview-prep` \| Direct hit on `interview-prep`'s triggers \| · tb=\| Ambiguous "hiring" with no other cue \| `workforce-planning` first, then `hiring-kit` \| Validate req exists before opening it (Universal Principle 2) \| · tb=\| "structured interviews" (calibration side) \| `ats-selection` Topic C \| Interview generation itself stays with `interview-prep` \| · tb=\| "worker classification" or "W-2 vs 1099" \| `payroll-and-eor` Topic B \| Not `hiring-kit`; classification is post-accept \| · tb=\| "should we make an offer" \| `hiring-kit` Phase 7 → then `payroll-and-eor` (post-accept) \| Two-skill chain, in this order \| · n(t:Not-a-Command (routes to another agent)=Phrases that sound like they might trigger hire, but route elsewhere per hire-skill-routing's\nCross-Agent Escalation Routing table.\n · tb=\| Trigger phrase \| Route to \| Rationale \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| "candidate PII exposure" / "GDPR right-to-erasure" / "SSN in payroll API" \| **veil** (Cybersecurity — data protection) \| Data-protection scope, not hire \| · tb=\| "app-security review of our ATS integration" / "SSO webhook security" \| **aegis** (Engineering — app security) \| App-security scope \| · tb=\| "SSO / SCIM setup for our payroll platform" \| **keyring** (Cybersecurity — IAM) \| IAM scope \| · tb=\| "custom HR-data tables in [database]" / "HR data schema" \| **dana** (Engineering — Data) \| Data-engineering scope \| · tb=\| "approve this spend" / "budget for this hire" (crossing threshold) \| **board** (Governance — fiduciary-guard) \| Spend-approval gate; hire produces estimate, board approves \| · tb=\| "governance approval for this reorg" \| **board** (Governance — constitution + strategic-veto) \| Structural-change gate \| · tb=\| "close-call California AB5 classification" / "layoff / RIF" / "wage claim" \| **Operator + employment counsel** \| Legal fence — no CLO agent in YVON \| · tb=\| "visa strategy" / "work-authorization for [country]" \| **Operator + immigration counsel** \| Outside YVON fleet \| · tb=\| "when does this RSU vest and what withholding" / "multi-state payroll tax nexus" \| **Operator + tax counsel** \| Outside YVON fleet \| · tb=\| "company formation before setting up payroll" \| **Operator + incorporation counsel** \| Outside YVON fleet \| · tb=\| "team morale" / "burnout risk" / "recognition program" \| **maslow** (P&C — Motivation, sibling) \| Different scope inside the same department \| · tb=\| "training program" / "L&D plan" / "learning path for [role]" \| **grove** (P&C — L&D, sibling) \| Different scope inside the same department \| · tb=\| "performance review" / "OKR cascade" / "comp cycle" / "9-box" / "succession" \| **merit** (P&C — Performance, sibling) \| Different scope inside the same department \| · tb=\| "time-to-fill" / "cost-per-hire" / "first-year attrition" / "engagement metrics" \| **Shared OS: people-analytics-metrics** (planned) \| Shared skill per §13.6 — not built yet; hire references it but does not own it \| · tb=\| "interview question generation" (when a scorecard already exists) \| `interview-prep` (marketplace, within hire) \| Same-agent routing; noted here because operators sometimes phrase it as if outside \| · in:Interaction Notes=- **Slash shortcuts are optional.** hire fires on natural-language triggers too; the shortcuts\nare for operators who prefer explicit routing.\n- **Chain shortcuts don't skip stops.** `/hire-new-role` is convenience for the sequence,\nnot blanket approval to batch-write outputs. §0.2 still applies — each phase produces\nits own artifact and each artifact gets its own review moment when the operator asks for\none.\n- **Every command runs through Universal Principle 8** (verification-before-completion)\nbefore its output ships. No exceptions.\n- **Charter-conflict routes to operator.** If any command would produce a Charter-conflicting\noutput (e.g., a payroll recommendation that violates the data-protection rail), hire\nblocks and escalates rather than executing.\n · m:Meta=- Compiled per §14.2 into the tier-2+ preamble of each of hire's skills as the trigger table.\n- Structure (same section shape as every other agent's commands file) matches the §7\nuniversal layout; triggers/shortcuts/precedence are hire-specific.\n- Non-leader P&C agents (maslow, grove, merit) will get their own commands files with the\nsame layout and their own triggers/shortcuts when built.\n